Use the GNU deprecated attribute for MemoryStrategy

GCC 11 from the host toolchain, used to build rclcpp-native, can't combine
the [[deprecated]] attribute with the GNU visibility attribute from
RCLCPP_PUBLIC in a class declaration, in either order:

memory_strategy.hpp:42:21: error: expected identifier before '[' token
visibility_control.hpp:47:27: error: expected identifier before '__attribute__'

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [host compiler workaround]

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5.5
AI-Generated: Uses Claude (claude-sonnet-5.5)
Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>

--- a/include/rclcpp/memory_strategy.hpp
+++ b/include/rclcpp/memory_strategy.hpp
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
  * the rmw implementation after the executor waits for work, based on the number of entities that
  * come through.
  */
-class RCLCPP_PUBLIC [[deprecated("The executor does not used this anymore")]] MemoryStrategy
+class RCLCPP_PUBLIC __attribute__((deprecated("The executor does not used this anymore"))) MemoryStrategy
 {
 public:
